WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.480
In the world of My Hero Academia, nearly 80
percent of the population have inborn superpowers

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.440
called quirks.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.460
These superpowers run the gamut from the standard
to the completely bizarre, but not all quirks

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.620
are created equal.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.020
Here are the worst and best quirks ranked.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.040
Minoru Mineta has the ability to throw giant
sticky balls that grow on his head in place

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:20.560
of hair.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.200
The balls stick to whatever surface they land
on, but Mineta himself bounces right off.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.210
Already, we're off to a bad start.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.460
The idea of throwing sticky balls that grow
out of your scalp is incredibly disturbing.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.060
The worst part, however, is the side effect
that comes from throwing too many of his hair

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:35.560
balls.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.580
If Mineta overuses his quirk, his head starts
to bleed, which implies that his balls are

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.740
closer in composition to skin than hair.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.220
All in all, it's a deeply disturbing quirk
that's gross enough to offset even the faintest

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.500
possibility of usefulness.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:53.620
It might seem strange for a quirk with so
few downsides to land on the tail-end of this

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:58.500
list, but by the same token, Mashirao Ojiro's
quirk has no upsides, either.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.440
It's just a tail.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.740
In fairness, it's a tail that he has enough
control over to whip around and smack villains

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:04.240
with.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.800
However, compared to the most powerful and
most bizarre quirks in My Hero Academia, his

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.660
superpower is just boring.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.160
In fact, the plainness of his Quirk is about
as much character as Ojiro gets.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.820
When your entire personality is rooted in
how boring your superpower is, that's when

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.940
you know you've lost the genetic lottery.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.980
Still, there's no need to live life with your
tail between your legs.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.340
Mirio Togata is one of the most impressive
heroes in My Hero Academia.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.640
Trained by the pro hero Nighteye and considered
one of the Big Three at U-A, Mirio seems to

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.140
be the platonic ideal of an All Might successor.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.540
Most impressively, he does it all with a Quirk
that's much worse than he makes it look.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:47.219
With his Permeation Quirk, Mirio can become
completely intangible; when he becomes tangible

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:50.900
inside of a solid object, he's rocketed out
of that object at high speed.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.740
You might be wondering why such a useful power
comes so low on the list.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:00.720
The reason is simple: Mirio goes blind, deaf,
and loses the ability to breathe when he phases.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.990
Basically, the only thing he feels is a vague
sense of falling, which, combined with his

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.060
tendency to phase into the ground, sounds
like pure torture.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.599
Spinner's quirk lets him stick to walls, but
that's because he's basically a lizard man.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:17.690
In a world where kids have navel lasers and
sugar-powered super-strength, the ability

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.020
to look like a big lizard just seems sad.

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:24.680
Some of the other characters have inherited
animal features, but they also get cool powers

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.240
of their own.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.120
Tokoyami has a bird head, but he also has
a shadow creature that can fly him around.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.600
Koda has a rock head, but he can talk to animals.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.840
Even another mutant, Tsuyu, has a long tongue,
acidic vomit, and can camouflage herself with

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.340
her surroundings.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.740
Compared to any of those, Spinner's ability
to look like the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtle

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.800
original character that you drew when you
were a teenager just doesn't measure up.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.580
The world of MHA is full of high-tech gadgets
and weird technology that heroes and villains

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.640
can use if they weren't lucky enough to be
blessed with an exceptionally useful quirk.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.680
Of course, someone has to design those interesting
gadgets and weapons, which is where Mei Hatsume

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.180
comes in.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:07.060
She attends U-A to learn how to make Support
Equipment, MHA's in-universe term for utility

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.720
belts, costumes, and super-weapons.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.939
It's no surprise that Hatsume's focus is on
the Support side of things since her quirk

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.200
is pretty boring.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.440
Hatsume's Zoom quirk lets her vision zoom
in any object that she's looking at up to

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.700
five kilometers away.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.980
It's not a bad quirk, but it's not really
a good one either.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.040
No wonder Hatsume chose a career path that
has almost nothing to do with it.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.200
Even in his old age, Gran Torino has proved
himself to be a powerful combatant multiple

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.840
times, and his Jet quirk seems to be a major
factor.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.600
It allows him to shoot air from the soles
of his feet, giving him incredible speed and

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.700
agility as he dashes around and delivers high-velocity
punches.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.800
So why isn't he higher on this list?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.840
As it turns out, that speed has to come from
somewhere.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.740
Gran Torino's quirk shoots air out of his
feet, but it's the same air he uses to breathe.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.020
That's some incredible lung strength, but
it means that there's a hard limit to how

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.200
often and how much he can use his quirk.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.710
Still, you could say that his quirk is a breath
of fresh air compared to the more outlandish

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:02.520
ones out there.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.200
Shoto Aizawa, a.k.a. Eraserhead can temporarily
halt the activation of quirks as long as he

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.560
keeps his eyes open after looking at a quirk
user.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.960
As soon as he blinks, the effect ends.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.580
It doesn't affect mutant types like Spinner
or Ojiro, but it would stop Todoroki from

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.000
controlling fire and ice.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.280
That's a pretty useful power in the world
of My Hero Academia, which is packed to the

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.500
brim with quirk users of all type.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.160
The ability to shut down a villain before
they start doing their villainous acts is

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.040
solid, but that's all it does.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.620
Ultimately, a quirk that depends so much on
the presence of other quirk users to be effective

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.280
makes this a middle-of-the-road power.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.650
Who among us can say that they've never stomped
through sand castles or miniature cities pretending

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:46.260
to breathe nuclear fire while humming Blue
Oyster Cult's second-best song?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.640
It's an enticing fantasy, and one that the
superhero Mt. Lady can live every day.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:56.480
As you might expect from her punny name, Mt.
Lady can grow to giant size with her Gigantification

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:56.980
quirk.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.740
Unfortunately, it's only half as useful as
it sounds.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.080
Mt. Lady can grow to giant size, but she doesn't
have the ability to grow and shrink; she only

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.970
has the ability to grow to her giant size
and back to regular human size.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:14.230
That seems like a recipe for disaster in metropolitan
areas, and the lack of control means that

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:19.300
Gigantification is unlikely to land in the
top spot of any Most Desired Superpower list.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.620
Still, we'd be lying if we said that we didn't
want to act out our own Tom Hanks in Big fantasies:

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.760
"I wish I were big."

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:34.380
We already have at least one super-speedster
in the My Hero Academia cast in the form of

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.560
U-A student Tenya Iida, but his Engine quirk
is still revving up in the anime.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:43.820
Instead, his brother, the pro hero Ingenium,
has a much more powerful quirk at the moment.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.300
Instead of powerful engines on his legs like
his younger brother, Ingenium has engines

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.110
on his arms, letting him blast through the
air like the world's fastest Naruto Runner.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.740
In other words, he's both fast and furious.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.389
"I live my life a quarter-mile at a time."

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:03.390
In the world of My Hero Academia, quirks usually
come with a drawback or weakness, but that's

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.860
not something Shoto Todoroki has to worry
about.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:10.120
His quirk allows him to control fire and ice
to an almost unlimited extent.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.980
On the right side of his body, he generates
ice, while on the left, he can control fire.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:19.490
Granted, overusing one half of his body reflects
that increase or decrease in temperature onto

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:23.120
his own body, but just switching to the other
half regulates his own temperature back to

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:23.800
normal.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.120
Even in the world of My Hero Academia, Todoroki's
quirk is absurdly powerful.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:33.170
In fact, its existence is explicitly due to
active effort on his father's part to engineer

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.640
an ultra-powerful heir.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:39.800
However, putting Todoroki's tragic superhero
origin aside, we can't find any particular

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.560
issue with this ultra-powerful quirk.

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:45.780
We're not going to play hot and cold here;
this quirk is worth getting fired up about.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.520
Copycat characters have existed in superhero
fiction almost as long as superpowers.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.830
From Taskmaster to Amazo, there's just something
innately satisfying about seeing someone copy

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.260
and combine familiar superpowers in new ways.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:02.960
Since My Hero Academia never shies away from
a good superhero fictional trope, there is,

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.100
of course, a copycat quirk wielder.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:10.040
The catch is that he's pretty undeniably heroic,
even if he's kind of a jerk about it.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.420
Neito Monoma is a U-A student with the ability
to copy the quirk of anyone he touches.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:19.680
He can copy up to four abilities, and use
any one ability at a time for up to ten minutes

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.940
before he needs to physically touch them again.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:26.380
While that's not much use out in the real
world, Monoma's Copycat quirk is extraordinarily

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.440
useful in the quirk-filled world of My Hero
Academia.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.460
Being able to copy up to four powers at a
time with a touch makes Monoma an incredibly

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.040
dangerous opponent in a melee.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:39.009
What's more, knowledge of his quirk only makes
him more dangerous, since he can throw in

00:07:39.009 --> 00:07:40.979
bluffs to confuse clever enemies.

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:45.099
The only real drawback to his quirk, besides
the time limit, is that he can only make use

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.750
of quirks that don't depend on external power
sources.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.920
Fat Gum's Fat Absorption quirk wouldn't be
possible for the skinny Monoma, and so on.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.000
A balanced diet is important to living your
best life.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:08:00.330
For Tamaki Amajiki, a balanced diet is particularly
important to living his best superhero life.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.900
As the hero Suneater, Tamaki has the ability
to manifest characteristics of whatever he

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.200
eats as a part of his own body.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:10.930
That means that if he eats clams or octopus,
he can turn parts of his body into tentacles

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:11.980
or clam shells.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.560
If he eats a bird, he can grow wings and fly.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:19.460
The size, number of manifestations, and exact
features of the food he wants to use are entirely

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.280
up to him.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:25.140
While it's an incredibly weird-looking quirk
to have, it's undeniably a useful one.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.400
Hit up an all-you-can-eat fish buffet, and
you could probably swim faster than Michael

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:29.900
Phelps.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:34.620
Eat a few plates of chicken, and you can,
uh, kind of halfway fly and hop around.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:39.040
You get the idea Tamaki's power isn't even
limited to conventional food, either.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:43.180
At one point, he eats some crystals created
by another quirk user in order to make his

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.300
own flesh into crystals.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:49.240
Best Jeanist's Fiber Master quirk allows him
to control individual threads of fiber.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:53.550
That makes him nearly unstoppable against
anyone wearing clothes, which is nearly everyone.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:55.220
"He's a never nude."

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.620
"Is that exactly what it sounds like?"

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:02.440
"Tobias suffered from a rare psychological
affliction of never being able to be completely

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:02.940
naked."

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.240
Best Jeanist has some minor drawbacks to his
quirk: for one, the type of thread influences

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:09.020
how easily he's able to control it.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.100
Still, it's one of the weirdest and most useful
quirks in all of the My Hero Academia universe.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.220
Unless he goes up against a supervillainous
nudist colony, Best Jeanist is one of the

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:18.720
best.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:23.540
Twice can make an exact duplicate of anything
as long as he knows the exact measurements.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:27.380
He's limited to two doubles at a time, and
those doubles are slightly weaker than the

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:30.700
real things, but they still have their own
abilities and will.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:34.970
That means that, functionally, he doesn't
have any limits when it comes to cloning himself.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:39.270
He can clone himself, and then that clone
can clone himself, and then that clone's clone

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.650
can clone himself, and so on infinitely.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:45.770
Beyond its use in making personal armies,
it's the perfect cooperative quirk with other

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.250
villains, since Twice can make a clone of
himself and a clone of another villain, which

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.680
can likewise repeat seemingly infinitely.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:56.220
In fact, the only real reason that My Hero
Academia isn't entirely about the world's

00:09:56.230 --> 00:10:01.270
heroes uniting against this seemingly ultra-powerful
villain is that Twice spends most of his time

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.300
completely insane as a result of cloning himself
too much.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:08.200
He didn't know if he was the original clone
and spent years worrying that he was just

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.260
his own doppelganger.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:14.320
As horrifying as that might be, there's a
pretty easy solution: just write numbers on

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:18.660
all your clones' heads, and it doesn't seem
like identity confusion will ever be a problem.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.030
“They look exactly like us, so in order
to avoid confusion I'm going to mark us each

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:23.460
with a red X right now."

